{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-immersion-into-noetherian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7da3f2eeab826c17562551196cad4d4662efdc535924c087f9b1b5aefdda0e10", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cf56640872385faf7323adac239d22c30b97cfb83b293925888a08b1b3efcd17", "source_text": "Any immersion <MATH_0001> with <MATH_0002> locally Noetherian is quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a9a95a97e3598614d1a3d134643f974e936d5760c3490a029ae3f19272f7c618", "unit_id": "tag:01OX:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-lemma-composition-quasi-compact}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-affine}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-Noetherian-topology}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{topology-lemma-Noetherian}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{topology-lemma-Noetherian-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2cdd54c91172842da7935e351b2e537dfc65808da525fec53dd82898c278104", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dd68080632a325526badd536b22cfec7b91c7b2fd1447981c1e59f483116ddcd", "source_text": "A closed immersion is clearly quasi-compact.\nA composition of quasi-compact morphisms is quasi-compact,\nsee Topology, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nHence it suffices to show that an open immersion into\na locally Noetherian scheme is quasi-compact.\nUsing Schemes, Lemma <REF_0002>\nwe reduce to the case where <MATH_0001> is affine.\nAny open subset of the spectrum of a Noetherian ring\nis quasi-compact (for example\ncombine Algebra, Lemma <REF_0003> and\nTopology, Lemmas <REF_0004> and\n<REF_0005>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1b55c48b18d9541c433c84755e39b6925db716a5c032f5439cbd373c1a2f5d5a", "unit_id": "tag:01OX:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-Noetherian-quasi-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b4e008d54cda55e944033542e08b36cb23d72e71a16aa188d561aefd7b2796a1", "source_text": "A locally Noetherian scheme is quasi-separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:87f85c85d09537541848166067fec36a5b8a1a079534bff9e092cd9bfc6e4afe", "unit_id": "tag:01OY:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U \\cap V$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\cap V \\to U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-characterize-quasi-separated}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-immersion-into-noetherian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:deb3d63ef1ab7d95b15ee444113ed87a168964ede03e3de805001ba0c6eab5ef", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1c02f68a383f3eb83740a22fd57a9279fdd94a3ec142aa025bd248d51cb7e5d5", "source_text": "By Schemes, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe have to show that the intersection <MATH_0001> of two\naffine opens of <MATH_0002> is quasi-compact. This follows from\nLemma <REF_0002> above on\nconsidering the open immersion <MATH_0003> for example.\n(But really it is just because any open of the spectrum of a\nNoetherian ring is quasi-compact.)\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:41ae8a4bc92a5219982d155aeb0b5cd1e892f36ba885745c03b41c26462957b2", "unit_id": "tag:01OY:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-definition-noetherian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-Noetherian-topology}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6680a634ebc4eaa45e92acb4fa1308605f500bbd85ae275ba852bf02e8c552f9", "source_text": "A (locally) Noetherian scheme has a (locally)\nNoetherian underlying topological space,\nsee Topology, Definition <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7e1dcd5361ee463e45f59fd9bc136bed4acd4f19535ea0b82c238f1458a7cf9e", "unit_id": "tag:01OZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01OU", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-Noetherian-topology}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topology-lemma-finite-union-Noetherian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2a9e082590b7e6963d2709bb1695000a0c27fd4feef20a2838e6be5bb2f94232", "source_text": "This is because a Noetherian scheme is a finite union of spectra\nof Noetherian rings and\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001> and\nTopology, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:646131a20035e5633513354feee4a172a360a1ec021c587fee02e5867834d3ca", "unit_id": "tag:01OZ:proof"}
